BLOCKS = [
    ('chapter', 'Part 3', 'The Prologue', 'From an owl at the window to the first night in a common room.'),
    ('p', 'The Prologue is four blocks on the clock: Letters arrive, Gringotts and Diagon Alley, the Hogwarts Express, and the Welcome Feast. '
          'It is the part of the game where the players learn that this world answers back. Everything they poke here should feel wonderful, '
          'and nothing should be dangerous yet. Save the fear for the castle.'),
    ('tip', 'The Prologue has no house points (nobody is sorted yet), so your rewards are Galleons, sweets and attention. A player who does something charming in Diagon Alley should get a moment in the spotlight for it.'),

    ('h2', 'Scene 1: The letter'),
    ('gm', 'The opening cutscene ends on the family page. When everyone has a family, Close the book. Table tab: choose Home, Just show on TV.'),
    ('read', 'Somewhere in Britain, on an ordinary morning at the end of summer, an owl lands where no owl should be. It is carrying a heavy envelope of yellowish parchment, addressed in emerald-green ink to someone who has never had a letter in their life. Or who has had hundreds, and none like this.'),
    ('p', 'Go round the table. The DM Guide has vignettes for the first six families. Here are the three newer ones.'),
    ('h3', 'Hale'),
    ('read', 'The owl lands on the windowsill of the consulting room while your mother is setting a broken wrist. She doesn’t even look up. “Open it, then. Carefully, it’s probably sealed with a charm.” It is. It smells faintly of St Mungo’s: clean linen and something green. Behind you, on the shelf, your great-grandmother’s casebook sits where it always sits. Today, for no reason, it has fallen open.'),
    ('h3', 'Penrose'),
    ('read', 'The owl arrives in the middle of a rehearsal and lands on the leading actor, who is your uncle, who is currently wearing the face of a king. Everyone stops. Your hair goes bright purple with excitement before you can stop it. Your grandmother reads the letter over your shoulder and says, “Hogwarts. Good. And for heaven’s sake, child, arrive looking like yourself.”'),
    ('h3', 'Okafor'),
    ('read', 'The owl taps at the workshop window, and your dad, a Muggle engineer, still jumps every single time. Your mum takes the letter from its leg without a word and runs her fingers over the wax seal, checking it for curses out of habit. Then she smiles and gives it to you. Later that night you hear her on the Floo, arguing with someone at Gringotts about a painting. She sounds frightened. She never sounds frightened.'),
    ('wait', 'For each player: “Tell us one thing about you that nobody at Hogwarts knows yet.” Write the answers down. You will use them all week.'),
    ('ifs', [
        ('They want to write back', 'Lovely. Their owl takes it. On Day 1 an owl brings a reply from home: a parent’s voice in two lines. Write it yourself with the Owl Post tab.'),
        ('They read their family secret aloud', 'Let them. Some players love to share. Then ask the table: “Does anyone else’s family have a story like that?”'),
        ('They try magic at home', 'Underage magic outside school: an owl from the Ministry arrives within a minute with a stern warning. It is funny, not a punishment.'),
    ]),

    ('h2', 'Scene 2: Gringotts'),
    ('gm', 'Day &amp; class tab: Advance time. Table tab: choose Gringotts, tick everyone, Move them here. Then open each vault from the Players tab.'),
    ('read', 'At the top of Diagon Alley stands a snowy-white building with bronze doors. Inside, the hall is marble and silence, and a hundred goblins sit at high desks weighing jewels and writing in ledgers, and every one of them looks up at you at once.'),
    ('say', 'Gringotts goblin', '“Vault keys. Or account names. Quickly.”'),
    ('table', ['Family', 'Vault', 'Say this as the door opens'], [
        ['Hale', '240 Galleons', '“Neat stacks of gold, and a Wiggenweld Potion your parents left on top with a note: Use it on someone else first.”'],
        ['Penrose', '180 Galleons', '“Gold, three theatre masks, and a costume nobody has worn in a hundred years.”'],
        ['Okafor', '280 Galleons', '“Gold, and a small brass curse-breaker’s pick your mum left for you. She would say it’s for emergencies. She would mean always.”'],
    ], [26, 26, 118]),
    ('p', 'The other six vaults are in the DM Guide.'),
    ('ifs', [
        ('They ride the mine cart', 'Of course they do. A goblin takes them down. It is fast, it is dark, it is the best thing that has ever happened to them. Anyone who rolls a natural 1 on a CON check is sick on arrival.'),
        ('They ask about other vaults', '“Gringotts does not discuss other customers.” A WIS 13 check notices one vault door covered in dust, with a serpent on the lock. The goblin sees them notice.'),
        ('They try to steal', 'There is no surer way to die. The goblin smiles with every one of his teeth. Do not let it get further than the thought.'),
        ('The Marlowe shows the serpent key', 'The goblin goes very still. “That key does not open anything at Gringotts.” Pause. “Anymore.”'),
    ]),

    ('h2', 'Scene 3: Diagon Alley'),
    ('gm', 'Header: 🛍️ Open shops. Move everyone to Diagon Alley. The Shop tab on their phones ticks off the school list.'),
    ('read', 'Diagon Alley swallows you whole. Cauldrons stacked outside shops, owls hooting in cages, a witch selling eyeballs by the jar, bunting strung between crooked chimneys. Every window wants you. At the far end of the street, a narrow, dusty shop has a single wand on a faded cushion in its window.'),
    ('p', 'Let them split up and shop. While they are busy with their phones, walk around and give each small group a moment:'),
    ('ifs', [
        ('They look in the bookshop', 'A book of monsters tries to bite them. A book of jokes laughs at its own jokes. A heavy book called “Painters of the Enchanted Canvas” is on the bargain table, and the shopkeeper says it has been returned three times.'),
        ('They visit the pet shop', 'Something in the back is purring very loudly. Every animal turns to look at the Thornbury. A toad escapes.'),
        ('They open barrels outside the apothecary', 'Beetle eyes, a Sickle a scoop. Dragon liver, not for children. One barrel is labelled “DO NOT OPEN” and has a small voice inside it saying “please open”. (It is a Fanged Frisbee. It goes for their ankles: DEX 10 or 1 HP.)'),
        ('They try to buy something not on the list', 'If it is reasonable, it exists. Price it at 3–10 Galleons and give the item, or a custom item with a name. A broomstick is 50 Galleons and first-years cannot have one at school.'),
        ('They help someone who can’t afford their list', 'Remember it. At the feast, or at the first chance once sorted, give the helper +5 house points.'),
        ('They are rude to a shopkeeper', 'The price goes up by a Galleon, and the shopkeeper tells the next shop.'),
    ]),
    ('h3', 'The rival'),
    ('read', 'Outside the pet shop, an older boy in expensive robes is leaning against the wall, tossing a Galleon. He looks at you like you are something on his shoe.'),
    ('say', 'Cassius Thorne', '“First-years. Lovely. Try not to cry in the Great Hall this year.”'),
    ('ifs', [
        ('They answer back', 'He smiles slowly. “Oh, I’m going to enjoy this year.” He remembers their name.'),
        ('They ignore him', 'He says the Marlowe’s surname loudly as he passes, so the whole street turns. Then he is gone.'),
        ('They hex him', 'He blocks it with a flick (he is three years older). “Cute.” A shopkeeper shouts. No points yet: nobody is sorted.'),
    ]),

    ('h2', 'Scene 4: Ollivanders'),
    ('read', 'A bell tinkles somewhere deep in the shop. The place smells of dust and old wood. Thousands of narrow boxes are piled to the ceiling, and some of them hum. Then an old man with wide, pale eyes is simply there, as if he has been standing behind the counter all along.'),
    ('say', 'Mr Ollivander', '“Ah. I wondered when I would be seeing you.”'),
    ('p', 'One student at a time. The Wand questions are on the Players tab; each student gets a different random set. Read them in his voice, and read his reply to each answer from the purple box on the GM panel or the Ceremony Book. While one student answers, the others will poke at the shop:'),
    ('ifs', [
        ('They open wand boxes', 'Every box they open, the wand inside does something: a shower of sparks, a vase explodes, their hair turns blue. Spin the Wand misfire wheel for fun.'),
        ('They climb the ladder', 'The ladder slides along the shelves by itself and stops exactly where Ollivander wants it. He does not turn round. “Third box from the left, if you would.”'),
        ('They ask about Vale', 'He goes quiet. “I sold a wand once to a painter. Rowan and unicorn hair. A gentle wand. He did not use it gently.” That is all.'),
        ('The Marlowe gets their wand', 'Ollivander says the line about the great-grandfather and the yew wand. Let it hang.'),
    ]),
    ('read', '“Curious,” Ollivander murmurs, as the wand warms in your hand. “The wand chooses the wizard, you see. It is not always clear why. But I think we can expect great things from you. Or terrible ones. Often it is the same thing.”'),

    ('h2', 'Scene 5: The platform and the train'),
    ('gm', 'Advance time to The Hogwarts Express. Move everyone to Platform Nine and Three-Quarters first, then to the Express.'),
    ('read', 'King’s Cross, eleven o’clock, and there is no platform nine and three-quarters. There is platform nine. There is platform ten. Between them is a solid brick barrier, and a family with an owl cage has just walked straight into it and vanished.'),
    ('wait', '“How do you get through?” The Quill has no idea. Whoever explains it to the Quill earns the first kindness of the campaign.'),
    ('ifs', [
        ('They walk at it slowly', 'They bump their nose. It is brick. You have to mean it.'),
        ('They run at it', 'Steam, noise, a scarlet engine. They are through.'),
        ('The Penrose changes face to look older', 'A guard waves them through without a ticket check. Nobody asked for one anyway.'),
    ]),
    ('read', 'The train pulls out of the station and the city falls away into green hills. You have a compartment to yourselves. Somewhere down the corridor, a trolley is rattling closer.'),
    ('p', 'The Express is the first place they can roam. Here is everything on it:'),
    ('ifs', [
        ('The trolley', '“Anything from the trolley, dears?” Chocolate Frogs, Pumpkin Pasties, Bertie Bott’s Beans, a Galleon each. Give the item and take the gold.'),
        ('Other compartments', 'Roll a d6: 1 a toad, escaped; 2 older students playing Exploding Snap (it explodes); 3 a girl reading upside down; 4 Prefect Sinclair; 5 Cassius and two friends; 6 an empty compartment, very cold, the window frosted on a summer day.'),
        ('The luggage racks', 'Trunks, cages, a broomstick someone smuggled. A small find if they search.'),
        ('Prefect Sinclair', 'She introduces herself and checks on her sibling. If the Sinclair talks to her alone, she admits the bad dreams.'),
        ('Cassius', 'He passes their compartment and greets the Marlowe by surname, loudly, for the whole carriage.'),
        ('The window', 'Hills, then mountains, then a lake. At dusk, the first sight of a castle on a cliff, every window lit.'),
        ('Pulling the emergency brake', 'Do not let it work. The handle is enchanted and simply goes “no” in a polite voice.'),
    ]),
    ('h3', 'The last carriage'),
    ('say', 'The trolley witch', '“Oh, don’t go back there, dear. Some delivery for the school. Gave me the shivers, and I’ve carried a dragon egg on this train.”'),
    ('read', 'Between the luggage racks of the last carriage, something large leans against the wall, wrapped in grey cloth and tied with cord. A painting, by the shape of it. There is no label. The cold in this carriage is the kind you feel in your teeth.'),
    ('p', 'Only the Quill sees the eye. Tell them alone, or quietly:'),
    ('read', 'The cloth has slipped at one corner. Through the gap, you see a painted eye. It blinks. It follows you as you step back. When you look again, the cloth is in place, as if it never moved.'),
    ('ifs', [
        ('The Okafor touches it', 'Their Curse-Breaker sense goes off like an alarm: something in there is alive, and very old, and paying attention. Exactly what their mother felt.'),
        ('The Blackwood asks it a question (Portrait Whisperer)', 'It does not answer. That has never happened before. Every Blackwood portrait has always answered.'),
        ('Anyone tries to unwrap it', 'See Part 1, the covered painting and spells. The cord is iron-tight.'),
        ('They tell Prefect Sinclair', 'She goes pale, then laughs it off. “Probably a portrait of some old headmaster.” She checks it herself later. She does not laugh about it again.'),
    ]),

    ('h2', 'Scene 6: The Sorting'),
    ('gm', 'Advance time to The Welcome Feast. Move everyone to The Great Hall. The Sorting Hat is on the Players tab, one student at a time. Each student hears five different questions; the Hat’s reply to every answer is in the purple box on the GM panel and in the Ceremony Book.'),
    ('read', 'The boats cross a black lake under a sky full of stars, and Hogwarts rises above you, every window lit. Inside is a hall so tall that its ceiling is the night sky itself. Thousands of candles float in the air. Four long tables full of students fall silent, and on a stool at the front sits a battered, patched old hat.'),
    ('p', 'Sort in alphabetical order by family name: Blackwood, Fenwick, Hale, Marlowe, Okafor, Penrose, Quill, Sinclair, Thornbury. The Hat’s song is in the DM Guide.'),
    ('ifs', [
        ('They argue with the Hat', 'The Hat enjoys it. “Oh, a debater. Ravenclaw would love you. Or Slytherin would use you.” The argument counts as the house wish.'),
        ('They try to cheat the questions', 'The Hat knows. “You are answering what you think I want to hear. Which tells me rather a lot.”'),
        ('A Penrose changes face under the Hat', 'The Hat laughs out loud. “I see under faces, child. That’s rather the point of me.” The hall laughs too. Good laughter.'),
        ('Two friends want the same house', 'Let the wish matter. The Hat says so out loud: “Loyalty to a friend. Noted.”'),
    ]),
    ('read', 'The Hat shouts the name of your house, and one of the four tables explodes into applause. You stumble to your seat, your ears still ringing.'),
    ('gm', 'Each sorting shows a crest reveal on the TV. Their house specialty (Gryffindor Nerve, Ravenclaw Wit, Slytherin Cunning, Hufflepuff Steadfast) switches on and appears on their phone’s Sheet.'),
    ('h3', 'The Welcome Feast'),
    ('read', 'Golden plates fill with food out of nowhere. Ghosts drift through the tables. When the last plate has cleared itself, the Headmaster rises, and the hall falls silent.'),
    ('say', 'The Headmaster', '“Welcome, all. A few notices. The Forbidden Forest is forbidden: the name was a clue. Curfew is at nine. Mr Filch reminds you that he has keys to every door in this castle. And this year we have a gift: Professor Ashgrove, our new Defence teacher, has generously added to the castle’s collection of portraits. Do say hello to them. Most of them like to talk.”'),
    ('ifs', [
        ('They watch the staff table', 'Ashgrove laughs with everyone. Grimsby eats alone and looks at no one. Vance taps her glass once. Flitwick is standing on his chair to see. A WIS 14 check: Ashgrove keeps glancing at the floor, as if listening to something underneath it.'),
        ('They talk to the ghosts', 'The ghost asks politely whether they have seen a large painting arrive. She seems relieved when they have not, and worried when they have.'),
        ('They try to sneak out of the feast', 'Prefects herd first-years like sheep. A DEX 15 gets them as far as the Entrance Hall, where Filch is waiting, delighted.'),
        ('They eat everything', 'Let them. Ask what their favourite dish is. It appears on their plate, twice.'),
    ]),

    ('h2', 'Scene 7: The first night'),
    ('gm', 'Table tab: 👩‍🏫 Send all staff to their rooms. Then 🛏️ Lights out sends everyone to their own common room. Advance time when you are ready: the first school day begins.'),
    ('p', 'Every common room has its own way in. Make each house do theirs once, in front of everyone. It makes the houses feel real.'),
    ('table', ['House', 'The way in', 'If they get it wrong'], [
        ['Gryffindor', 'The Fat Lady’s portrait asks for the password. A prefect tells them on the first night.', 'She refuses and sings at them until they leave.'],
        ['Ravenclaw', 'No password: a bronze eagle knocker asks a riddle. Make one up, or use: “What has a neck but no head?” (A bottle.)', 'The knocker asks another. They can wait for someone cleverer.'],
        ['Hufflepuff', 'Tap the right barrel near the kitchens, twice, then once, in the right rhythm.', 'The wrong barrel sprays them with vinegar.'],
        ['Slytherin', 'Say the password to a bare stone wall in the dungeons.', 'Nothing. The wall waits. The lake sloshes behind it.'],
    ], [26, 86, 58]),
    ('ifs', [
        ('They explore the common room', 'See Part 5 for each room. Every common room has someone in it with gossip: spin Portrait gossip, or tell them a rumour about the new paintings.'),
        ('They sneak out on night zero', 'Nothing is hunting yet, but Filch is. Spin Out after curfew. It is a great way to get detention on the first night and start The Old Cup early.'),
        ('They go to bed', 'Ask each player one question: “What do you dream about?” The Quill dreams of a painted eye. Tell them so.'),
    ]),
]
